  "runtime_rules": [
    "Profiles provide context and limits; they do not generate dialogue by themselves.",
    "An NPC may only use dialogue knowledge allowed by its knowledge_tags plus story-state gates.",
    "STORY_OVERRIDE and DANGER_OVERRIDE always outrank ambient schedule phases.",
    "Named NPC schedules may be sparse when film-story placement controls their location.",
    "Ambient archetypes may use cheap aggregate schedules and must not require persistent per-instance memory.",
    "Aliases refer to the same identity and must not create duplicate persistent memories.",
    "Relationship data cannot alter mandatory film story outcomes.",
    "Named story profiles may expose biography_facts and knowledge_limits to local dialogue context, but those fields never override story-state gates.",
    "Every profile, including ambient archetypes, participates in the offline living-NPC layer at a cost appropriate to its persistence tier.",
    "Regional world mood is shared context for all NPCs and may influence dialogue/behavior without changing mandatory story outcomes."
